The sealed W02 packet supports one narrow inherited-name correction. The bare `Hemodal` entry in selected Menadione `d18105cf` does not provide enough context to resolve uniquely to neutral menadione. This conclusion rests on positive evidence of distinct chemical forms, not merely on the ontology's BRAND NAME annotation or absent historical product details.

I read the complete selected and authentic-before records, their original proposal/case/evidence context, the four-token matrix, final skeptic/readback qualifications, and the cited primary sections. Both records contain the same `Hemodal / EXACT_SYNONYM / kg_microbe` object. The exact W08 published payload and proposal blobs and A842 before blob match. The original operation remains `ORIGINAL-w08::vm-prop-menadione`; no new source case or origin is needed to describe the issue.

| Token | Bounded disposition supported by inspected evidence |
|---|---|
| Aquakay | Retain the documented neutral-menadione chemical-name sense. NIST molecular record and Sangon A502486 SDS sections 1/3 connect the name with CAS58-27-5. This does not identify every historical finished product. |
| Aquinone | Retain the documented chemical-name sense. NIST and the captured Santa Cruz sc-205990 synonym/composition sections support neutral menadione. Historical injection composition is not inferred. |
| Hemodal | Change only the inherited unqualified entry to a nonresolving disposition if root selects the correction. Preserve its positive neutral-name usage and all original text/source/history. |
| Kappaxin | Retain the documented chemical-name sense. KEGG D02335 and LKT V3479 SDS sections 1/3 give menadione, C11H8O2 and CAS58-27-5. A historical injection listing does not establish whole-product equivalence. |

For Hemodal, the captured Santa Cruz sc-205990 and sc-215295 primary sections 1/3 both use the token but identify neutral menadione CAS58-27-5 and menadione sodium bisulfite CAS130-37-0 respectively. I read the exact browser-extracted text in `research/c/search-07.json`; the separately retained curl failure bodies are not misrepresented as successful PDF captures. I also visually inspected the preserved Bayer advertisement image from original Coimbra Médica February 1945 PDF page22. Its tablet derivative and sodium-bisulfite injection are distinct labeled blocks. The complete source PDF `691a9d0f` and page image `2a1a5d83` are hash-bound. No new Bayer fetch or backdated acquisition is claimed.

MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 requires claim-specific evidence for a new REJECTED_LABEL. This evidence is sufficient for the unqualified inherited assertion. The native representation can be `synonyms[synonym_text=Hemodal].synonym_type: REJECTED_LABEL`, keeping `synonym_text` and `source: kg_microbe` unchanged and appending truthful evidence/history explaining ambiguity and positive neutral-name usage. This rejects unconditional resolution of the sourced entry, not every use of the word or the known Menadione substance. RAW_TEXT would not express the required nonresolving state. A SUPPRESS decision would require another resolved preferred owner and its own native credits; no such owner assignment is made here. No replacement identifier, bisulfite record creation, invented structure, mapping-status change or blanket brand-name rejection follows.

The correction must start from selected `d18105cf`, not authentic-before `2ffe65c6`, to retain the accepted ATCC1257 solute alias and its history. Preserve all other synonyms, CHEBI:28869/CAS58-27-5, formula/structure, roles, counts, source-case and original-proposal objects, and the distinction between 50mg solute and the separate ethanol/water stock. The flattened source dose remains unvalidated. Later validation must prove only this one resolution removal and truthful provenance additions, including a negative against reintroduction through KG synonyms. Root filed the exact finding on #718 comment6724713374 before any correction; the actual filing packet is bound separately below.

Collection is complete: 185 regular manifest members (52,018,417 bytes), exact ignored-inclusive membership plus three declared control files, strict native YAML/derived Markdown, all184 native source inputs, four original context containers and original/copy/Git joins pass. The native review remains `needs_curation`, science limited to the four token claims. Its source is the actual W02 c91 working-tree attestation. It used native primitives and a private overlay, with `canonical_save_review_used: false`; this receipt does not relabel it as a saved production review or a fresh whole-owner approval.

Independence is qualified rather than multiplied. W02's root/research_b/research_c authored the synthesis; its final_reviewer inspected the recommendations and also supplied a source lead/shared captures. Prior Mc participation included scientific work as clarified in the final readback, but did not author these four inherited entries. These are W02-internal identities, not coordinator A/B/C identities. Shared sources are evidence, not separate approval votes. The pending W01 whole-row review is not included as an approval. This collection/triage makes no source, role, row, export or application decision, and does not modify the already-reviewed four-correction input selection.

Local collector limitations are preserved: an initial optional PyMuPDF import was unavailable; available `pdftotext` was used for the original LKT/Sangon sections, and the existing Bayer image was read visually. The first collector assumed the wrong manifest key, and a preparatory context inspection assumed every context container had one locator. Both were collector shape errors before any source write, not W02 defects. Their failed logs and original collector are retained; the corrected collector reads the actual `members` schema and both singular/plural context forms. No broad validation or source generation was run.
